  'You are given a problem. Think about the problem and provide your reasoning. Place it between <reasoning> and </reasoning>. Then, provide the final answer (i.e., just one numerical value) between <answer> and </answer>.\n\nAmaya scored 20 marks fewer in Maths than she scored in Arts. She also got 10 marks more in Social Studies than she got in Music. If she scored 70 in Maths, then how many marks did she get in Arts?\n\n{reasoning}Let the marks scored by Amaya in Maths be x.\n\nThen the marks scored by Amaya in Arts be x-20.\n\nThe marks scored by Amaya in Music be (x-20)+10.\n\nNow, we know that Amaya scored 70 in Maths, which implies that x=70.\n\nTherefore, the marks scored by Amaya in Arts be x-20=70-20=50.\n\nHence, Amaya scored 50 marks in Arts.{/reasoning}\n\n{answer}50{/answer}\n\n{reasoning}Let the marks scored by Amaya in Maths be x.\n\nThen the marks scored by Amaya in Arts be x-20.\n\nThe marks scored by Amaya in Music be (x-20)+10.\n\nNow, we know that Amaya scored 70 in Maths, which implies that x=70.\n\nTherefore, the marks scored by Amaya in Arts be x-20=70-20=50.\n\nHence, Amaya scored 50 marks in Arts.{/reasoning}\n\n{answer}50{/answer}<eos>'
