  "I will solve the problem step by step.\nGiven:\n- $a^2 - b^2 = 12$\n- $a^4 + b^4 = 82$\nWe need to find:\n- $a^6 - b^6$\nLet's start by squaring both sides of the equation $a^2 - b^2 = 12$:\n$a^2 - b^2 = 12$\n$(a - b)(a + b) = 12$\n$(a - b)(a + b) = 12$\n$a^2 + ab - ab - b^2 = 12$\n$a^2 + 0 = 12$\n$a^2 = 12$\n$a = \\pm\\sqrt{12}$\nNow, let's square both sides of the equation $a^4 + b^4 = 82$:\n$a^4 + b^4 = 82$\n$(a^2 + b^2)(a^2 - b^2) = 82$\n$(a^2 + b^2)(a^2 - b^2) = 82$\n$a^4 + a^2b^2 - ab^2 - b^4 = 82$\n$a^4 - b^4 = 82$\n$a^4 - b^4 = 82$\nNow, we can substitute $a = \\pm\\sqrt{12}$ into the equation $a^4 - b^4 = 82$:\n$(\\pm\\sqrt{12})^4 - b^4 = 82$\n$12 - b^4 = 82$\n$b^4 = 82 - 12$\n$b^4 = 70$\n$b = \\pm\\sqrt{70}$\nNow, we can find $a^6 - b^6$:\n$a^6 - b^6 = (\\pm\\sqrt{12})^6 - (\\pm\\sqrt{70})^6$\n$a^6 - b^6 = 12^6 - 70^6$\n$a^6 - b^6 = 1728 - 4900000$\n$a^6 - b^6 = -4899999$\nThe final answer is $a^6 - b^6 = -4899999$.\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n\\endgroup\n