  'You are given a problem. Think about the problem and provide your reasoning. Place it between <reasoning> and </reasoning>. Then, provide the final answer (i.e., just one numerical value) between <answer> and </answer>.\n\nWe are given that $a^2-b^2=12$ and $a^4+b^4=82$. We want to find $a^6-b^6$.model\nWe know that:model\n$a^2-b^2=12$model\n$a^4+b^4=82$model\nWe can rewrite the second equation as:model\n$a^4=82-b^4$model\nNow we can substitute this value into the first equation:model\n$a^2-(82-b^4)^2=12$model\n$a^2-6561+b^4=12$model\n$a^2+b^4=6439$model\nNow we can take the square root of both sides:model\n$\\sqrt{a^2+b^4}=\\sqrt{6439}$model\n$a^2+b^4=251$model\nNow we can substitute this value into the first equation:model\n$a^2-12=251$model\n$a^2=263$model\nNow we can take the square root of both sides:model\n$\\sqrt{a^2}=\\sqrt{263}$model\n$a=\\pm\\sqrt{263}$model\nNow we can substitute this value back into the second equation to find $b^4$:model\n$b^4=82-\\left(\\pm\\sqrt{263}\\right)^4$model\n$b^4=82-263\\left(263\\right)$model\n$b^4=82-69349$model\n$b^4=-69267$model\nNow we can take the square root of both sides:model\n$\\sqrt{b^4}=\\sqrt{-69267}$model\n$b^4=\\pm\\sqrt{-69267}$model\n$b^4=\\pm\\sqrt{69267}$model\n$b^4=\\pm9\\times11\\times3\\times3\\times19\\times19$model\n$b^4=\\pm9\\times11\\times3\\times19\\times3\\times19$model\n$b^4=\\pm9\\times11\\times19\\times19$model\n$b^4=\\pm9\\times11\\times381$model\n$b^4=\\pm3027\\times11$model\nNow we can substitute this value back into the first equation:model\n$a^2+b^4=251$model\n$a^2+3027\\times11=251$model\n$a^2=251-33287$model\n$a^2=-32836$model\nNow we can take the square root of both sides:model\n$\\sqrt{a^2}=\\sqrt{-32836}$model\n$a=\\pm\\sqrt{-32836}$model\n$a=\\pm\\sqrt{32836}$model\n$a=\\pm57$model\nNow we can substitute this value back into the second equation to find $b^4$:model\n$b^4=82-\\left(\\pm57\\right)^4$model\n$b^4=82-32836$model\n$b^4=-32754$model\nNow we can take the square root of bot