led with water, and the pool is drained at a rate of 20 liters per minute, how long will it take to completely drain the pool?\n\n<strong>Answer:</strong> 20 minutes\n\n<strong>Reasoning:</strong> The volume of the swimming pool is equal to the length * width * height, which is 20 * 10 * 10 = 2000 liters. If the pool is filled with water, and the pool is drained at a rate of 20 liters per minute, the pool will be completely drained in 2000/20 = 100 minutes.\nYou are given a problem. Think about the problem and provide your reasoning. Place it between <reasoning> and </reasoning>. Then, provide the final answer (i.e., just one numerical value) between <answer> and </answer>.\n\nA rectangular swimming pool is 20 meters long and 10 meters wide. If the pool is filled with water, and the pool is drained at a rate of 20 liters per minute, how long will it take to completely drain the pool?\nYou are given a problem. Think about the problem and provide your reasoning. Place it between <reasoning> and </reasoning>. Then, provide the final answer (i.e., just one numerical value) between <answer> and </answer>.\n\nIn a certain country, 30% of the population is over the age of 65. If there are 5000 people over the age of 65, how many people are in the country?\nYou are given a problem. Think about the problem and provide your reasoning. Place it between <reasoning> and </reasoning>. Then, provide the final answer (i.e., just one numerical value) between <answer> and </answer>.\n\nA rectangle has a length of 10 units and a width of 5 units. The rectangle is divided into 1000 smaller rectangles each with a length of 1 unit and a width of 0.5 units. What is the area of the smallest rectangle in square units?\nYou are given a problem. Think about the problem and provide your reasoning. Place it between <reasoning> and </reasoning>. Then, provide the final answer (i.e., just one numerical value) between <answer> and </answer>.\n\nIn a certain country, 30% of the population is over t