  'You are given a problem. Think about the problem and provide your reasoning. Place it between <reasoning> and </reasoning>. Then, provide the final answer (i.e., just one numerical value) between <answer> and </answer>.\n\nA sphere is inscribed in a cone with a base radius of 6 cm and a height of 20 cm. The volume of the sphere is 288π cm^3. What is the ratio of the radius of the sphere to the radius of the cone\'s base? Express your answer as a common fraction.\n<reasoning>\nThe volume of a sphere is given by <tex>$$V = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi r^3$$</tex>. The volume of the cone is given by <tex>$$\\frac{1}{3}Bh$$</tex>, where <tex>$B$</tex> is the area of the base and <tex>$h$</tex> is the height. The area of the base is <tex>$$\\pi r^2$$</tex>, so <tex>$$V = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi r^3 = \\frac{1}{3}Bh$$</tex>. Simplifying, we get <tex>$$r^3 = \\frac{3}{4}r^2h$$</tex>. Solving for <tex>$h$</tex>, we get <tex>$$h = \\frac{4}{3r^2}$$</tex>.\n</reasoning>\n<answer>\n<span style="font-size: 14pt;">The ratio of the radius of the sphere to the radius of the cone\'s base is <span style="font-size: 14pt;">\\(\\frac{r}{\\frac{r}{\\frac{4}{3r^2}}}\\)</span>, which simplifies to <span style="font-size: 14pt;">\\(\\frac{3}{4}\\)</span>.</span>\n</answer>\nYou are given a problem. Think about the problem and provide your reasoning. Place it between <reasoning> and </reasoning>. Then, provide the final answer (i.e., just one numerical value) between <answer> and </answer>.\n\nA sphere is inscribed in a cone with a base radius of 6 cm and a height of 20 cm. The volume of the sphere is 288π cm^3. What is the ratio of the volume of the sphere to the volume of the cone? Express your answer as a common fraction.\n<reasoning>\nThe volume of a sphere is given by <tex>$$V = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi r^3$$</tex>. The volume of the cone is given by <tex>$$\\frac{1}{3}Bh$$</tex>, where <tex>$B$</tex> is the area of the base and <tex>$h$</tex> is the height. The area of the base is <tex>$$\\pi r^2$$</tex>, so <tex>$$V = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi r^3 = \\frac{1}{3}Bh$$</tex>. Simplifying, we get <tex>$$r^3 = \\frac{3}{4}r^2h$$</tex>. Solving for <tex>$h$</tex>, we get <tex>$$h = \\frac{4}{3r^2}$$</tex>.\n</reasoning>\n<answer>\n<span style="font-size: 14pt;">The ratio of the volume of the sphere to the volume of the cone is <span style="font-size: 14pt;">\\(\\frac{r^3}{\\frac{3}{4}r^2h}\\)</span>, which simplifies to <span style="font-size: 14pt;">\\(\\frac{4}{3}\\)</span>.</span>\n</answer>\nYou are given a problem. Think about the problem and provide your reasoning. Place it between <reasoning> and </reasoning>. Then, provide the final answer (i.e., just one numerical value) between <answer> and </answer>.\n\nA sphere is inscribed in a cone with a base radius of 6 cm and a height of 20 cm. The volume of the sphere is 288π cm^3. What is the ratio of the volume of the cone to the volume of the sphere? Express your answer as a common fraction.\n<reasoning>\nThe volume of a sphere is given by <tex>$$V = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi r^3$$</tex>. The volume of the cone is given by <tex>$$\\frac{1}{3}Bh$$</tex>, where <tex>$B$</tex> is the area of the base and <tex>$h$</tex> is the height. The area of the base is <tex>$$\\pi r^2$$</tex>, so <tex>$$V = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi r^3 = \\frac{1}{3}Bh$$</tex>. Simplifying, we get <tex>$$r^3 = \\frac{3}{4}r^2h$$</tex>. Solving for <tex>$h$</tex>, we get <tex>$$h = \\frac{4}{3r^2}$$</tex>.\n</reasoning>\n<answer>\n<span style="font-size: 14pt;">The ratio of the volume of the cone to the volume of the sphere is <span style="font-size: 14pt;">\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\frac{4}{3r^2}\\)</span>, which simplifies to <span style="font-size: 14pt;">\\(\\frac{1}{3r}\\)</span>.</span>\n</answer>\nYou are given a problem. Think about the problem and provide your reasoning. Place it between <reasoning> and </reasoning>. Then, provide the final answer (i.e., just one numerical value) between <answer> and </answer>.\n\nA sphere is inscribed in a cone with a base radius of 6 cm and a height of 20 cm. The volume of the sphere is 288π cm^3. What is the ratio of the area of the sphere to the area of the cone\'s base? Express your answer as a common fraction.\n<reasoning>\nThe area of a sphere is given by <tex>$$A = 4\\pi r^2$$</tex>. The area of the cone\'s base is given by <tex>$$\\pi r^2$$</tex>.\n</reasoning>\n<answer>\n<span style="font-size: 14pt;">The ratio of the area of the sphere to the area of the cone\'s base is <span style="font-size: 14pt;">\\(\\frac{4\\pi r^2}{\\pi r^2}\\)</span>, which simplifies to <span style="font-size: 14pt;">\\(\\frac{4}{1}\\)</span>, or 4.</span>\n</answer>\nYou are given a problem. Think about the problem and provide your reasoning. Place it between <reasoning> and </reasoning>. Then, provide the final answer (i.e., just one numerical value) between <answer> and </answer>.\n\nA sphere is inscribed in a cone with a base radius of 6 cm and a height of 20 cm. The volume of the sphere is 288π cm^3. What is the ratio of the surface area of the sphere to the surface area of the cone\'s base? Express your answer as a common fraction.\n<reasoning>\nThe surface area of a sphere is given by <tex>$$S = 4\\pi r^2$$</tex>. The surface area of the cone\'s base is given by <tex>$$\\pi r^2$$</tex>.\n</reasoning>\n<answer>\n<span style="font-size: 14pt;">The ratio of the surface area of the sphere to the surface area of the cone\'s base is <span style="font-size: 14pt;">\\(\\frac{4\\pi r^2}{\\pi r^2}\\)</span>, which simplifies to <span style="font-size: 14pt;">\\(\\frac{4}{1}\\)</span>, or 4.</span>\n</answer>\nYou are given a problem. Think about the problem and provide your reasoning. Place it between <reasoning> and </reasoning>. Then, provide the final answer (i.e., just one numerical value) between <answer> and </answer>.\n\nA sphere is inscribed in a cone with a base radius of 6 cm and a height of 20 cm. The volume of the sphere is 288π cm^3. What is the ratio of the volume of the sphere to the volume of the cone\'s ba