  "<model>\n<problem>\n<problem_text>\nA sphere is inscribed in a cone with a base radius of 6 cm and a height of 20 cm. The volume of the sphere is 288π cm^3. What is the ratio of the radius of the sphere to the radius of the cone's base?\n</problem_text>\n<answer>\n<answer_text>\n0.375\n</answer_text>\n</answer>\n<reasoning>\n<reasoning_text>\nThe radius of the cone's base is 6 cm, and the height of the cone is 20 cm. The volume of the cone is 0.75 * π * 20^2 = 300π cm^3. The volume of the sphere is 288π cm^3, so the ratio of the radius of the sphere to the radius of the cone's base is:\n\n288π cm^3 / 300π cm^3 = 0.96\n\nTherefore, the ratio is approximately 0.96.\n</reasoning_text>\n</reasoning>\n</problem>\n</model><eos>"
