  'A company has a budget of $300,000 for advertising. They are considering two different options:\nOption A: Spend $100,000 on TV advertising and $200,000 on radio advertising.\nOption B: Spend $150,000 on TV advertising and $150,000 on radio advertising.\nIf they want to maximize the amount of advertising they can do, which option should they choose?\nIn order to find the maximum amount of advertising, we need to find the point of the graph where the slope is 0. The slope of the line for Option A is:\n<tex>$\\displaystyle \\frac{\\text{Change in y}}{\\text{Change in x}} = \\frac{200,000 - 100,000}{200,000 - 100,000} = \\frac{100,000}{100,000} = 1$</tex>\nThe slope of the line for Option B is:\n<tex>$\\displaystyle \\frac{\\text{Change in y}}{\\text{Change in x}} = \\frac{150,000 - 150,000}{150,000 - 150,000} = \\frac{0}{0} = \\text{Undefined}$</tex>\nThis means that the slope of the line for Option B is undefined, which means that the line is vertical. In order to find the maximum amount of advertising, we need to find the point of the graph where the slope is 0. The point of the graph where the slope is 0 is (150,000, 150,000). This means that if we choose Option B, we will spend $150,000 on TV advertising and $150,000 on radio advertising, which will give us the maximum amount of advertising that we can do.\n<strong>Answer: Option B</strong>\n<strong>Step-by-step explanation:</strong>\n<strong>Answer:</strong>\n<strong>Explanation:</strong>\nThe graph of a quadratic function is a parabola, which is a symmetrical U-shaped curve. The axis of symmetry of the parabola is the line that passes through the vertex and is perpendicular to the x-axis. The focus of the parabola is the point on the parabola that is closest to the vertex. The directrix of the parabola is the line that is parallel to the axis of symmetry and is a distance away from the vertex.\nThe equation of the parabola is:\n<tex>$\\displaystyle (x - h)^2 = 4p(y - k)$</tex>\nWhere (h,k) is the vertex and p is the distance from the vertex to the focus.\nThe axis of symmetry is the line that passes through the vertex and is perpendicular to the x-axis.\nThe equation of the axis of symmetry is:\n<tex>$\\displaystyle x = h$</tex>\nThe focus is the point on the parabola that is closest to the vertex.\nThe equation of the focus is:\n<tex>$\\displaystyle x = x_f + p$</tex>\nWhere x_f is the x-coordinate of the focus.\nThe directrix is the line that is parallel to the axis of symmetry and is a distance away from the vertex.\nThe equation of the directrix is:\n<tex>$\\displaystyle y = k - p$</tex>\nWhere k is the y-coordinate of the vertex.\nIn order to find the x-coordinate of the focus and the distance from the vertex to the focus, we need to find the equation of the axis of symmetry and the equation of the parabola.\nThe equation of the axis of symmetry is:\n<tex>$\\displaystyle x = h$</tex>\nThe equation of the parabola is:\n<tex>$\\displaystyle (x - h)^2 = 4p(y - k)$</tex>\n<tex>$\\displaystyle (x - h)^2 = 4p(y - k)$</tex>\n<tex>$\\displaystyle x^2 - 2hx + h^2 = 4py - 4pk$</tex>\n<tex>$\\displaystyle x^2 - 2hx + h^2 = 4py - 4pk$</tex>\n<tex>$\\displaystyle x^2 - 2hx + h^2 = 4py - 4pk$</tex>\n<tex>$\\displaystyle x^2 - 2hx + h^2 = 4py - 4pk$</tex>\n<tex>$\\displaystyle x^2 - 2hx + h^2 = 4py - 4pk$</tex>\n<tex>$\\displaystyle x^2 - 2hx + h^2 = 4py - 4pk$</tex>\n<tex>$\\displaystyle x^2 - 2hx + h^2 = 4py - 4pk$</tex>\n<tex>$\\displaystyle x^2 - 2hx + h^2 = 4py - 4pk$</tex>\n<tex>$\\displaystyle x^2 - 2hx + h^2 = 4py - 4pk$</tex>\n<tex>$\\displaystyle x^2 - 2hx + h^2 = 4py - 4pk$</tex>\n<tex>$\\displaystyle x^2 - 2hx + h^2 = 4py - 4pk$</tex>\n<tex>$\\displaystyle x^2 - 2hx + h^2 = 4py - 4pk$</tex>\n<tex>$\\displaystyle x^2 - 2hx + h^2 = 4py - 4pk$</tex>\n<tex>$\\displaystyle x^2 - 2hx + h^2 = 4py - 4pk$</tex>\n<tex>$\\displaystyle x^2 - 2hx + h^2 = 4py - 4pk$</tex>\n<tex>$\\displaystyle x^2 - 2hx + h^2 = 4py - 4pk$</tex>\n<tex>$\\displaystyle x^2 - 2hx + h^2 = 4py - 4pk$</te