  'You are given a problem. Think about the problem and provide your reasoning. Place it between <reasoning> and </reasoning>. Then, provide the final answer (i.e., just one numerical value) between <answer> and </answer>.\n\nA teacher has a bag of 30 different colored marbles. The bag contains an equal number of red, green, and blue marbles. If 10 of the marbles are red, how many green marbles are there?\n\n<reasoning>The teacher has 10 red marbles and the rest are green and blue. We know that there are an equal number of red and green marbles, so there are 10 green marbles.</reasoning>\n\n<answer>15</answer>\n</code><eos>'
