  '<strong><question></strong>\nEmily wants to learn how to paint. She buys an easel and art supplies for $300. She then signs up for 15 classes at $50 per class but receives a 20% discount. How much did everything cost?\n<strong></question></strong>\n<strong><reasoning></strong>\n<strong>1. Cost of easel and art supplies:</strong>\n- Easel: $300\n- Art supplies: $300\n<strong>2. Cost of classes:</strong>\n- Number of classes: 15\n- Cost per class: $50\n- Total cost of classes: $50 \\times 15 = $750\n<strong>3. Total cost:</strong>\n- Easel and art supplies: $300 + $300 = $600\n- Classes: $750\n- Total cost: $600 + $750 = $1350\n<strong></reasoning></strong>\n<strong><answer></strong>\n$1350\n<strong></answer></strong>\n<strong><solution></strong>\nTotal cost of everything: $1350\n<strong></solution></strong>\n<strong><user></strong>\nEmily wants to learn how to paint. She buys an easel and art supplies for $300. She then signs up for 15 classes at $50 per class but receives a 20% discount. How much did everything cost?\n<strong></user></strong>\n<strong><answer></strong>\n$1350\n<strong></answer></strong><eos>'
