  'The user must write their own code to solve the problem and provide the final answer. The user must provide their code and the final answer in the form of a valid mathematical expression. The final answer must be a common fraction.\n<user>\n\n<code>import random\n\ndef is_same_rank(card1, card2):\n    return card1[0] == card2[0] and card1[1] == card2[1]\n\ndef count_same_rank(deck):\n    same_rank_count = 0\n    for card in deck:\n        for other_card in deck:\n            if card != other_card and is_same_rank(card, other_card):\n                same_rank_count += 1\n    return same_rank_count\n\ndef draw_cards(deck, count):\n    result = []\n    for i in range(count):\n        card = random.choice(deck)\n        result.append(card)\n    return result\n\ndef main():\n    deck = [\n        (card[0], card[1]) for card in [\n            (0, \'Ace\'), (0, \'King\'), (0, \'Queen\'), (0, \'Jack\'), (0, \'Ten\'),\n            (1, \'Ace\'), (1, \'King\'), (1, \'Queen\'), (1, \'Jack\'), (1, \'Ten\'),\n            (2, \'Ace\'), (2, \'King\'), (2, \'Queen\'), (2, \'Jack\'), (2, \'Ten\'),\n            (3, \'Ace\'), (3, \'King\'), (3, \'Queen\'), (3, \'Jack\'), (3, \'Ten\'),\n        ]\n    ]\n    count = 5\n    same_rank_count = count_same_rank(deck)\n    result = draw_cards(deck, count)\n    print(f"The probability that the cards are of the same rank is {same_rank_count / count:.2f}")\n    print(f"The cards drawn are: {result}")\n\nif __name__ == "__main__":\n    main()\n</code>\n\n</user>\n<reasoning>\nTo solve the problem, we need to draw cards from the deck and count the number of cards that are of the same rank. We can do this by using the random module to select a card from the deck and adding it to a list. We then need to check if the card is of the same rank as the card we have already selected. If it is, we add it to a count variable. After we have drawn enough cards, we can calculate the probability that the cards are of the same rank by dividing the number of cards of the same rank by the total number of cards in the deck.\n</reasoning>\n<answer>\nThe probability that the cards are of the same rank is <common_fraction(same_rank_count / count)>.\n</answer>\n</solution><eos>'
