  'You are given a problem. Think about the problem and provide your reasoning. Place it between <reasoning> and </reasoning>. Then, provide the final answer (i.e., just one numerical value) between <answer> and </answer>.\n\nThe perimeter of a square is 100 meters. The width of the square is 10 meters more than the length. What is the length of the square?\n\n<strong>Answer</strong>: 20 meters\n<strong>Reasoning</strong>: We can represent the length of the square as L, and the width as W.\nWe are given that the perimeter of the square is 100 meters, which means that the sum of the sides is 100 meters.\nWe can write an equation for the perimeter:\n<strong>L + L + W + W = 100</strong>\nSimplifying this equation, we get:\n<strong>2L + 2W = 100</strong>\nWe are also given that the width of the square is 10 meters more than the length, which means that the width is W + 10.\nWe can substitute this value of W into the equation:\n<strong>2L + 2(W + 10) = 100</strong>\nSimplifying this equation, we get:\n<strong>2L + 2W + 20 = 100</strong>\nCombining like terms, we get:\n<strong>2L + 2W = 80</strong>\nWe can solve this equation for L:\n<strong>2L = 80 - 2W</strong>\n<strong>L = (80 - 2W) / 2</strong>\n<strong>L = 40 - W</strong>\nNow we can substitute this value of L into the equation for the perimeter:\n<strong>2(40 - W) + 2W = 100</strong>\nSimplifying this equation, we get:\n<strong>80 - 2W + 2W = 100</strong>\nCombining like terms, we get:\n<strong>80 = 100</strong>\nThis is not possible, which means that there is an error in our reasoning.\n\n<strong>Answer</strong>: The width of the square is 20 meters.\n<strong>Reasoning</strong>: We need to consider the possibility that there is an error in our reasoning.\nIt is possible that the perimeter of the square is not 100 meters, but 105 meters.\nIn this case, the width of the square would be 15 meters.\nWe can substitute this value of W into the equation:\n<strong>2L + 2(W + 10) = 100</strong>\nSimplifying this equation, w